CREATED:20260529T184939Z
DESCRIPTION:Everything You Wanted To Know About Collaborating Using Git an
 d GitHub But Were Afraid to Ask!\n\nInterested in learning how to use Git
  and GitHub to manage collaborations? Curious what this whole GitHub thin
 g is actually about? Join us for a three-part\, zero-prior-knowledge-requ
 ired workshop series led by Nick Eubank\, faculty director in the Duke Ma
 ster in Interdisciplinary Data Science (MIDS) program.\n\nParticipants wi
 ll be introduced to the command line (promise - it's not as scary as it s
 ounds!)\, Git\, and GitHub\, and learn how these tools can streamline pro
 fessional collaborations\, improve research reproducibility\, and open th
 e door to a wide range of resources and workflows used across academia an
 d industry.\n\nThe sessions build on one another\, so participants must a
 ttend the sessions that precede any later session.\n\nWorkshop Schedule\n
 \nThursday\, June 4\, 9:00-11:00 a.m.\nThursday\, June 4\, 1:00-3:00 p.m.
 \nFriday\, June 5\, 2:00-4:00 p.m.\nLocation: Gross Hall 230E\n\nAdvance 
 RSVP is required
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20260529T184939Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260604T090000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260529T184939Z
